; ============================================================
; TITLE:    String Art
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     straight lines, curves, FOR, SETXY, color
; SUMMARY:  Makes curves from nothing but straight lines, like string stretched between nails.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Imagine nails along two sides of a board. Stretch a string from
;   the first nail on one side to the last on the other, then the
;   second to the second last, and so on. The strings are straight,
;   yet together they make a smooth curve. This program does that in
;   all four corners of a square, each in its own color.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change :nails at the bottom for more or fewer strings.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * FOR loops that count nails
;   * SETXY to draw a line between two exact points
;   * how many straight lines can look like a curve
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use 10 nails, then 40. Which looks smoother?
;   * Only draw two opposite corners.
;   * Use black strings on a white background.
; ============================================================

; STRING stretches one string from (x1, y1) to (x2, y2).
to string :x1 :y1 :x2 :y2
  penup setxy :x1 :y1 pendown
  setxy :x2 :y2
end

; CORNER fills the corner between two sides that meet at (cx, cy).
; The nails run along the x side and the y side of the corner.
; :dx and :dy say which way the sides go: 1 or -1.
to corner :cx :cy :dx :dy :color
  setpencolor :color
  for [k 0 :nails] [
    localmake "gap :k * :size / :nails
    string :cx + :dx * :gap :cy :cx :cy + :dy * (:size - :gap)
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [20 20 40]
setpensize 1.5
make "nails 30
make "size 260
corner 0 0 1 1 [255 100 120]
corner 0 0 -1 1 [255 200 80]
corner 0 0 -1 -1 [90 200 255]
corner 0 0 1 -1 [140 230 120]
